---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Workshops — Ruijie Wu" description="Embodied workshops and learning spaces shaped by movement, attention and relationship.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Workshops &amp; learning / 03</span>
    <h1>Thinking through<br /><em>movement.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Spaces to explore the body as a source of expression, relationship, imagination and knowledge.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="workshop-intro container">
    <div class="workshop-quiet-mark">A space<br />to move<br />and notice.</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>These spaces are not about dancing well or producing a beautiful result. They invite participants to notice what movement makes possible, experiment at their own pace, and discover forms of expression that may not begin with words.</p>
      <p>No dance experience is required unless a particular programme says otherwise. Participation is invitational: observing, pausing or adapting an activity are all valid ways to take part.</p>
      <p>Each workshop is shaped in response to its group, setting and purpose. The outline below describes areas of practice rather than a fixed programme.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Ways of working</span>
      <div class="practice-list">
        <article><span class="number">01</span><div><h2>Body awareness</h2><p>Attending to sensation, breath, posture, weight and the body's changing relationship with space.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="number">02</span><div><h2>Emotion &amp; gesture</h2><p>Exploring how feelings may be sensed, expressed or transformed through qualities of movement.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="number">03</span><div><h2>Movement narratives</h2><p>Using gesture, rhythm, image and improvisation to approach personal or collective stories with choice and care.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="number">04</span><div><h2>Group process</h2><p>Noticing distance, connection, boundaries and the possibilities of moving alongside others.</p></div></article>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>Discuss a workshop or collaboration <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>